  {
    "pattern_id": "p2-action-success-stagnation",
    "severity": "medium",
    "description": "Recent RSIC cycles show that exactly half of all actions executed per cycle succeed (2/4 or 6/8 successful each cycle), with the remainder not failing but apparently not succeeding. No actions are recorded as explicit failures, but neither are they successfully completed, indicating possible action selection or detection issues.",
    "recommended_action": "review_guidance_effectiveness",
    "reasoning": "The consistent 50% action success rate, with no recorded failures, suggests actions are being attempted that are neither advancing nor failing—possibly being skipped, pre-empted, or aborted due to unclear criteria or stale trigger logic. Reviewing guidance effectiveness can help ensure action selection and completion criteria are well-aligned, and missed successes (or soft-failures) are made explicit for better control."
  },
  {
    "pattern_id": "p3-training-readiness-stalls",
    "severity": "medium",
    "description": "Several LLM training tasks (especially 'jiminy.codegen', 'jiminy.synthesize', and 'hidden.name_emergence') remain not ready for significant durations, with low daily completion rates and high accumulated error counts despite recent data. In particular, 'hidden.name_emergence' has an extremely high projected time-to-ready, suggesting it is effectively stalled.",
    "recommended_action": "archive_ineffective_constraints",
    "reasoning": "Stalled or extremely slow-developing training-readiness in specific tasks can point to overly strict or ineffective constraints/prompts. Archiving such constraints can help break deadlocks and encourage action re-selection, especially for bottlenecked or low-volume emergent-tasks like name emergence or synthesis."
  },
  {
    "pattern_id": "p4-task_performance-stability-low",
    "severity": "medium",
    "description": "Task performance remains low (0.10) and shows no notable improvement over multiple cycles, with other health and retrieval metrics remaining high. This indicates the system is healthy at the structural level but not progressing in task-level functional output.",
    "recommended_action": "codify_constraint",
    "reasoning": "The lack of task performance improvement despite overall health may indicate that constraints are too loose or insufficiently specified for current goals. Codifying and tightening performance-related constraints may encourage the system to focus on actions that directly drive task metric improvements."
  }
]

